WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.812 --> 00:00:07.150
-Imagine Alice traveled back
over 50,000 years to find

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.593
her distant ancestor, Bob.

00:00:14.976 --> 00:00:18.071
Now up until this time,
human culture was relatively

00:00:18.071 --> 00:00:21.365
unsophisticated, utilizing
the same primitive stone

00:00:21.365 --> 00:00:24.941
tools which went unchanged
for thousands of years.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:29.316
But somewhere around
50,000 years ago, something

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:31.289
interesting happened, and nobody

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.950
knows for sure why.

00:00:34.506 --> 00:00:37.469
There was a sudden explosion
of diverse cultural

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:40.557
artifacts, including
instruments for making music,

00:00:40.557 --> 00:00:44.087
new tools, and other forms
of creative expression.

00:00:44.396 --> 00:00:48.346
(foreign singing)

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:51.535
-Humans developed the
ability to externalize

00:00:51.535 --> 00:00:53.258
their inner thoughts.

00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:56.731
They began to communicate using language.

00:00:57.572 --> 00:01:01.050
So Alice begins her search
by looking for water.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.069
She knows that human and
animal populations tend to

00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:06.742
migrate towards and along rivers which are

00:01:06.742 --> 00:01:09.016
the life blood of ecosystems.

00:01:09.394 --> 00:01:12.345
Eventually she comes across
an interesting marking,

00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:14.529
Bob's hand print.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.985
This marking contains very
little information, simply

00:01:17.985 --> 00:01:20.761
that he was here and
could possibly return.

00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:25.486
Alice knows Bob is equally
intelligent, he can

00:01:25.486 --> 00:01:28.203
communicate orally, although
his culture has not yet

00:01:28.203 --> 00:01:30.460
developed the ability to read or write

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:32.367
in their native language.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.929
At the time, the universal
written language was art.

00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:39.830
So she finds natural
materials around her to paint

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.319
him a picture in case he returns.

00:01:42.646 --> 00:01:45.614
She renders an animal
she is tracking, hoping

00:01:45.614 --> 00:01:47.881
this will offer a clue
about the direction she

00:01:47.881 --> 00:01:49.834
is traveling in the future.

00:01:51.687 --> 00:01:54.931
Our ancestors used natural
materials to create

00:01:54.931 --> 00:01:58.134
pictorial representations
of their reality.

00:01:58.335 --> 00:02:00.668
Here is an actual cave
painting from around

00:02:00.668 --> 00:02:04.222
30,000 years ago, found
preserved deep inside

00:02:04.222 --> 00:02:06.314
Chauvet cave in France.

00:02:06.863 --> 00:02:08.338
Similar renderings are found in

00:02:08.338 --> 00:02:10.230
the caves of Spain as well.

00:02:11.061 --> 00:02:13.607
A common theme among
these ancient paintings

00:02:13.607 --> 00:02:16.819
are animals forms, as
well as the human hand,

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:20.790
perhaps a signature, a
story, or a ritual calling.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:25.130
-When Bob returns to the
waterfall, he finds her

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.944
painting and proceeds
towards the river where he

00:02:27.944 --> 00:02:29.544
thinks she might be.

00:02:30.812 --> 00:02:33.514
When he arrives, he does not find her,

00:02:33.806 --> 00:02:36.686
though he finds a sign
that she was here before.

00:02:38.368 --> 00:02:40.546
He decides to paint her a
picture explaining where

00:02:40.546 --> 00:02:43.720
he is going next, which
is halfway up the river

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.504
towards the setting sun.

00:02:45.953 --> 00:02:48.236
He has little time to
paint a picture as night is

00:02:48.236 --> 00:02:51.412
approaching, therefore
he needs a fast way to

00:02:51.412 --> 00:02:53.288
visualize his message.

00:02:53.598 --> 00:02:56.131
He thinks about it for a
moment and realizes his

00:02:56.131 --> 00:02:59.576
message only contains three
distinct mental objects,

00:03:00.314 --> 00:03:03.160
middle, river, west.

00:03:03.626 --> 00:03:05.369
So, he decides to use simplified

00:03:05.369 --> 00:03:07.276
pictures to represent them.

00:03:07.594 --> 00:03:10.186
For river, he draws a
symbol which resembles

00:03:10.186 --> 00:03:14.750
its natural form, known
as a Pictogram, which is

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.619
a drawing that resembles the physical

00:03:16.619 --> 00:03:18.649
object it represents.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.113
Pictograms are an important step

00:03:22.113 --> 00:03:24.051
in the evolution of writing.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.813
Here is a ceremonial slate
palette found in Egypt,

00:03:27.813 --> 00:03:30.292
dated before 3,000 BC.

00:03:30.652 --> 00:03:32.912
The surrounding scene
shows the struggle between

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:36.969
civilized humans and the
wild and ferocious animals.

00:03:39.622 --> 00:03:41.737
However, it's difficult
to draw pictures of

00:03:41.737 --> 00:03:46.687
abstract concepts, such
as calm, old, dangerous,

00:03:46.687 --> 00:03:48.979
or in Bob's case, middle.

00:03:49.651 --> 00:03:52.965
For this, he draws a line
with a box over the middle.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:55.088
It represents halfway.

00:03:55.499 --> 00:03:58.584
This is known as an
Ideogram, or conceptual

00:03:58.584 --> 00:04:00.897
picture of an abstract idea.

00:04:01.264 --> 00:04:03.893
Here's an example of this
same symbol on an ancient

00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:06.265
Chinese bronze inscription.

00:04:07.457 --> 00:04:09.902
For the idea of West,
he decides on a picture

00:04:09.902 --> 00:04:11.471
of the setting sun.

00:04:12.662 --> 00:04:14.785
Now he does something interesting.

00:04:15.765 --> 00:04:18.174
He combines these individual
symbols in terms of

00:04:18.174 --> 00:04:20.726
their meaning to create a message.

00:04:20.803 --> 00:04:24.094
Meaning plus meaning equals new meaning.

00:04:24.357 --> 00:04:26.929
He leaves this in hope
of Alice finding it.

00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:31.081
-Some of the earliest
artifacts of this symbolic

00:04:31.081 --> 00:04:34.374
merging are found in ancient Mesopotamia,

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:37.962
now modern Iraq, home of the Sumerians.

00:04:37.962 --> 00:04:40.535
This is the birthplace
of many of the world's

00:04:40.535 --> 00:04:42.706
earliest civilizations.

00:04:42.853 --> 00:04:45.814
Here we find clay accounting
tablets, which are some

00:04:45.814 --> 00:04:49.121
of the oldest written
documents ever found,

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:51.816
some dating before 3,000 BC.

00:04:51.816 --> 00:04:53.863
The rectangular tablets
record the payments

00:04:53.863 --> 00:04:56.715
in cattle, shipments of
cattle to shepherds for

00:04:56.715 --> 00:04:59.891
fattening, and gifts of
cattle as an offering.

00:04:59.957 --> 00:05:02.586
Notice that instead of
drawing a picture of 10 sheep,

00:05:02.586 --> 00:05:05.736
they draw a symbol
representing 10, using small

00:05:05.736 --> 00:05:08.983
notches, and another symbol
representing sheep or

00:05:08.983 --> 00:05:12.219
donkey, meaning simply 10 sheep.

00:05:12.327 --> 00:05:14.525
We call this Protowriting.

00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:17.058
Finally, Alice returns
to the base of the river

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.511
and finds Bob's message.

00:05:19.511 --> 00:05:21.819
She interprets the meaning correctly,

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:25.009
halfway West, down the river.

00:05:25.931 --> 00:05:28.998
So she marches down river
towards the setting sun,

00:05:28.998 --> 00:05:31.540
and eventually they finally meet.

00:05:32.309 --> 00:05:35.302
-Over time, Bob learns to
speak Alice's language,

00:05:35.302 --> 00:05:37.857
allowing them to use the
same oral language to

00:05:37.857 --> 00:05:40.767
communicate shared concepts and ideas.

00:05:42.052 --> 00:05:45.361
This gives them an
idea, the root of a more

00:05:45.361 --> 00:05:47.376
powerful written language.

00:05:47.477 --> 00:05:51.127
It starts with something very
simple, writing her name.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:54.827
She disassociates the
sound from the picture

00:05:54.996 --> 00:05:59.996
for her name Alice, Alice, Al-ice.

00:06:02.335 --> 00:06:05.316
She combines the
mathematical symbol for all,

00:06:05.316 --> 00:06:07.239
and a picture of ice.

00:06:07.529 --> 00:06:09.282
All ice.

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.709
Al-ice.

00:06:12.697 --> 00:06:14.449
Notice her name has nothing to do with the

00:06:14.449 --> 00:06:16.156
individual symbols.

00:06:16.492 --> 00:06:19.740
Sound plus sound equals new meaning.

00:06:20.077 --> 00:06:22.476
This is known as the Rebus principle.

00:06:23.004 --> 00:06:24.966
-A great example of
this was found in Egypt

00:06:24.966 --> 00:06:26.658
along the Nile River.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.681
Dated to around 3,100 BC,
it contained some of the

00:06:29.681 --> 00:06:33.312
earliest hieroglyphic
inscriptions ever found.

00:06:33.312 --> 00:06:35.439
The Narmer Palette depicts the Egyptian

00:06:35.439 --> 00:06:36.840
pharaoh, Narmer.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:39.160
On the back we see him
to the left of a kneeling

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:42.573
prisoner who's about the
be struck down by Narmer,

00:06:42.573 --> 00:06:45.505
who we see standing tall, wearing a crown.

00:06:46.286 --> 00:06:48.795
What we are looking for
is on the other side,

00:06:48.795 --> 00:06:51.431
between the two bovine
heads at the top, we see

00:06:51.431 --> 00:06:53.878
an inscription of his name.

00:06:53.899 --> 00:06:57.406
It's written as a fish and a chisel, which

00:06:57.406 --> 00:07:02.406
translates to Nar Mer,
Narmer, two sounds, separated

00:07:03.068 --> 00:07:05.658
from the pictures together,
giving new meaning.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.704
A key development in
the history of written

00:07:07.704 --> 00:07:10.439
language, but before they
could advance towards

00:07:10.439 --> 00:07:13.319
what we know of as an alphabet, something

00:07:13.319 --> 00:07:14.631
had to happen.

00:07:14.631 --> 00:07:16.784
They needed to save time.

